> Thanks Adam.  A lot of very good info there and quite clear.  Having never
> configured for a Proxy it seems quite simple.  A couple of little questions
> though if I may:
> 
> Would I have to configure all my applications such as Real Player,
> MailWasher, Firewall, AV etc. to use the same Proxy or can they use the
> default one and just my browser use the different proxy?
> 
> Does geographical location make much difference?  I'm in S Wales, but, seem
> to use Guilford cache-9, would using the Cardiff cache server be better?
> 
> Rob

Ok how it works is this...
If you don't select a proxy at all, then all trafic to port 80 goes via
whichever proxy NTL have selected for your address, so all of your web
browsing will be done via that proxy.
If on the other hand you explicitly choose a proxy in the browser settings
then it will use that instead.
Configure all of your other applications to take their settings from the
browser, if they don't have that setting then either leace them alone or
just pick one that works and change it if it breaks.
There really is no more science to it than that.
Adam


