Dear Aieie, & list:

Well, the PWS 500a will support Tru64, all the way up to 5.1 b.  The
main diff is, you set the console to SRM instead of AlphaBios.  From
AlphaBios, F2, then bios, the F6 (special).  You will get to a place
where you can swith consoles.  Pick Unix, save and get out.  You know
you did right when, next boot, you get a blue screen with a >>> prompt.


The SRM console has problems with Adaptec SCSI cards.  If you use them,
you need to boot from anotehr device, a floppy or bootable CD.  A
better move is eBay:  find a Qlogic 1020 or 1040 card, which SRM just
lo-o-o-ves.  $20 is an OK price.

Late model PWS, as Reinhard mentioned, have the Qlogic chipset on-board
and the scsi connector is on the mo-bo.
persist with your PWS, and good luck

jn

